2098:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * @return Value read from the receive FIFO. \n
2099:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * 			\b Range: 16bit data. Length of data depends on the word length configuration.
2100:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  *
2101:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * \par<b>Description</b><br>
2102:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * Gets data from the receive FIFO. \n\n
2103:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * Receive FIFO should be read only if data is availble in the FIFO. This can be checked using
2104:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * the API XMC_USIC_CH_RXFIFO_IsEmpty(). Receive FIFO error flag will be set if an attempt is made
2105:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * to read from an empty receive FIFO. To read all the received data, user should keep reading data
2106:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * until receive FIFO is empty.
2107:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  *
2108:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * \par<b>Related APIs:</b><BR>
