 623:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @brief Registers a request for transmitting data over I2C channel using DMA.
 624:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 625:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  handle  I2C_MASTER APP handle pointer of type @ref I2C_MASTER_t
 626:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  block_size size of the block
 627:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  addr    address\n
 628:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \b Range: minimum= 1, maximum= 4095.
 629:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 630:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @return  I2C_MASTER_STATUS_t: Status of transmit request.\n
 631:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *                        @ref I2C_MASTER_STATUS_SUCCESS if the request is accepted.\n
 632:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *                        @ref I2C_MASTER_STATUS_BUSY if a transmission is in progress.\n
 633:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 634:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * <i>Imp Note:</i> Return value should be validated by user to ensure that the
 635:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * request is registered.
 636:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 637:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
 638:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * The data transmission is accomplished using DMA. User can configure a callback function in the A
 639:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * When the data is fully transmitted, the callback function will be executed. The function uses AP
 640:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * structure to store the status of transmission.
 641:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * This function only registers a data transmission request, if there is no active transmission in 
 642:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Actual data transmission happens through DMA channel.
 643:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * A maximum of 4095 bytes can be transmitted in one API call. This limit is because of the DMA sin
 644:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Callback function is executed when all the data bytes are transmitted.
 645:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * If a callback function is not configured, user has to poll for the value of \a tx_busy flag of
 646:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * the APP handle structure( \a handle->runtime->tx_busy ) to check for
 647:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * the completion of data transmission.
 648:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * If data more than the block size of 4095 have to be transmitted, user will have to transmit them
 649:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * calls to this API.
 650:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>NOTE: </b><br>
 651:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * I2C_MASTER_StartTransmitDMA API can be used in DMA mode.
 652:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Transmit should be configured as "DMA" mode in advanced settings tab. \n
 653:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Address(addr) should reserve an additional bit at the LSB for read/write indication. For example
 654:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * be provided as 0x0a. If the address is 10-bit, only most significant bits with the 10-bit identi
 655:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * For example, if the 10-bit address is 0x305, the address should be provided as 0xf6(prepend with
 656:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * followed by 1-bit field for read/write).<br>
 657:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Example Usage:
 658:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 659:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @code
