 789:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h **** /**
 790:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @brief Registers a request for transmitting data over I2C_MASTER channel.
 791:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 792:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  handle  I2C_MASTER APP handle pointer of type @ref I2C_MASTER_t
 793:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  send_start flag to indicate the start condition
 794:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  address slave address
 795:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  data    pointer to buffer
 796:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  size    number of bytes
 797:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  send_stop flag to indicate the stop condition\n
 798:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \b Range: minimum= 1, maximum= maximum supported by uint32_t.
 799:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 800:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @return  I2C_MASTER_STATUS_t: Status of transmit request.\n
 801:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *                        @ref I2C_MASTER_STATUS_SUCCESS if the request is accepted.\n
 802:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *                        @ref I2C_MASTER_STATUS_BUSY if a transmission is in progress.\n
 803:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 804:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * <i>Imp Note:</i> Return value should be validated by user to ensure that the
 805:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * request is registered.
 806:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 807:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
 808:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * The data transmission is accomplished using transmit interrupt. User can configure a callback fu
 809:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * When the data is fully transmitted, the callback function will be executed. If transmit FIFO is 
 810:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * the trigger limit is set to 1. So the transmit interrupt will be generated when all the data in 
 811:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * from FIFO. The function uses APP handle's runtime structure to store the data pointer, count, da
 812:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * status of transmission. This function only registers a data transmission request if there is no 
 813:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * in progress.
 814:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Actual data transmission happens in the transmit interrupt service routine. A trigger is generat
 815:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * interrupt to start loading the data. If transmit FIFO is configured, the data is filled into the
 816:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Transmit interrupt will be generated next time when the transmit FIFO is empty. At this point of
 817:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * some more data to be transmitted, it is loaded to the FIFO again. When FIFO is not enabled, data
 818:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * byte at a time. On transmission of each byte an interrupt is generated and the next byte is tran
 819:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * interrupt service routine. Callback function is executed when all the data bytes are transmitted
 820:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * If a callback function is not configured, user has to poll for the value of \a tx_busy flag of t
 821:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * structure( \a handle->runtime->tx_busy ) to check for the completion of data transmission.<br>
 822:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>NOTE: </b><br>: I2C_MASTER_StartTransmitIRQ API can be used only in Interrupt mode.
 823:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Transmit should be configured as "Interrupt" mode in advanced settings tab.\n
 824:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Address(address) should reserve an additional bit at the LSB for read/write indication. For exam
 825:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * be provided as 0x0a. If the address is 10-bit, only most significant bits with the 10-bit identi
 826:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * For example, if the 10-bit address is 0x305, the address should be provided as 0xf6(prepend with
 827:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * followed by 1-bit field for read/write).
 828:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 829:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @code
 830:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 831:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *  #include "DAVE.h"
 832:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *  #define SLAVE_ADDRESS 0xA0
 833:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *  uint8_t tx_buffer[64] = {0x01,0x02,0x03,0x04,0x05};
 834:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *  uint8_t mem_address[2];
 835:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 836:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *  int main(void)
 837:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *  {
 838:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *    DAVE_STATUS_t init_status;
 839:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *    init_status = DAVE_Init();
 840:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *    if(init_status == DAVE_STATUS_SUCCESS)
 841:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *    {
 842:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *      mem_address[0] = 0x00;//memory which need to be read from slave
 843:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *      //Write data to IO EXPANDER
 844:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *      I2C_MASTER_StartTransmitIRQ(&I2C_MASTER_0,true,SLAVE_ADDRESS,mem_address,1,false);
 845:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *      while(I2C_MASTER_IsTxBusy(&I2C_MASTER_0));
