 865:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @brief Registers a request for receiving data over I2C_MASTER channel.
 866:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 867:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 868:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  handle  Pointer to I2C_MASTER_t handle structure
 869:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  send_start flag to indicate the start condition
 870:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  address slave address
 871:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  data    pointer to buffer
 872:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  count    number of bytes
 873:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  send_stop flag to indicate the stop condition
 874:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @param  send_nack flag to indicate the nack condition\n
 875:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \b Range: minimum= 1, maximum= maximum value supported by type uint32_t.
 876:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 877:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @return  I2C_MASTER_STATUS_t: Status for receive request.\n
 878:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *                        @ref I2C_MASTER_STATUS_SUCCESS if the request is accepted.\n
 879:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *                        @ref I2C_MASTER_STATUS_BUSY if a reception is in progress.\n
 880:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 881:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 882:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
 883:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Data will be received asynchronously. When the requested number of data bytes are received, opti
 884:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * configured callback function will be executed. Based on the UI configuration, either standard re
 885:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * receive FIFO is used for data reception. An interrupt is configured for reading received data fr
 886:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * function only registers a request to receive a number of data bytes from a USIC channel. If FIFO
 887:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * reception, the FIFO limit is dynamically configured to optimally utilize the CPU load.  When all
 888:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * of data bytes are received, the configured callback function will be executed. If a callback fun
 889:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * configured, the user has to poll for the value of the variable, \a handle->runtime->rx_busy to b
 890:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * is updated to \a false when all the requested number of data bytes are received.<br>
 891:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>NOTE: </b><br>: I2C_MASTER_StartReceiveIRQ API can be used only in Interrupt mode.
 892:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Receive should be configured as "Interrupt" mode in advanced settings tab.\n
 893:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Address(address) should reserve an additional bit at the LSB for read/write indication. For exam
 894:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * be provided as 0x0a. If the address is 10-bit, only most significant bits with the 10-bit identi
 895:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * For example, if the 10-bit address is 0x305, the address should be provided as 0xf6(prepend with
 896:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/TOF/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * followed by 1-bit field for read/write).
